# Pairs with StrictAdmitsOnlyServable in SchemaCrossRegion. Anti-entropy repair re-ships a row
# the receiver lacks and stores it directly, around strict ingest, so a body the receiver's
# policy refuses is admitted by repair where the stream would have diverted it.
MODULE: StrictAdmitsOnlyServableRepairSkipsJudgement
TARGET: StrictAdmitsOnlyServable
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: anti-entropy repair stores the source row verbatim, bypassing strict ingest
PERTURBS: Repair

--- FIND
    /\ IF dl[e] = 1 THEN UNCHANGED <<st, tag, dl>> ELSE Ingest(e, FALSE)
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the repaired row is stored without being judged.
    /\ st' = [st EXCEPT ![e] = Landing(e)]
    /\ tag' = [tag EXCEPT ![e] = stamp[e]]
    /\ UNCHANGED dl
--- END